# Files that decide what counts as proved. CI runs a pull request's own copies of these, so
# a change to any of them can weaken the check that judges it; each needs a review from a
# maintainer. This takes effect once the main branch's protection rule requires review
# from code owners.
#
# - the axiom sweep, its baseline, and the kernel replay
# - the style linter and its exceptions (the `native_decide` / kernel-bypass check)
# - the build configuration, which declares those executables, and the toolchain and
#   dependency lock, which decide what compiles them
# - the CI workflows that run them, and this file
